 "short_name": "Great Kei",
 "_doc": "Great Kei Local Municipality (Komga, Eastern Cape). FINGERPRINT: the municipality's own VAT number as printed in the masthead ('Municipality VAT Nr: <number>') plus the masthead name or its e-mail domain. Shared 'Computer Generated Tax Invoice For : <Month> - <Year>' statement (same print stream as Joe Gqabi/Ubuntu family, but the per-service layout: centred service heading, dated charge lines with Excl/VAT/Incl columns, a Sub Total per service, 'Total Levies for the Month'). Header block: Account Number, Property Physical Address with Consumer Deposit Cash/Guarantee and Statement Date on one line, Due Date, Invoice Number. Electricity section = the 'Electricity' heading down to its own Sub Total line (may run across a page break). Meter blocks come in two prints: (A) 'Physical Meter Nr / Tariff / Curr = .. Prev = .. Cons = .. / Reading Dates / Electricity Consumption: X KWH|KVA' with amounts on that line; (B) 'Reading dates: Cur .. Prev .. / Cur .. Prev .. Cons X KWH|KVA / Meter / Factor / qty x rate = amount / Tariff' with the amounts on their own line (tariff-change prorations print an extra reading-less block; a block is demand when it reads KVA or its tariff says KVA, else energy). total_ex_vat_r = sum of the electricity charge lines excl VAT with 'Interest' lines left out (interest is VAT-free arrears interest, kept in sbt_el_interest_r); standard_r = kWh charges, demand_r = kVA charges, other_r = the rest (basic/fixed). IDENTITY: total_ex_vat_r vs the printed electricity Sub Total excl-VAT column (sbt_el_sub_ex), which the system prints without the interest lines. Water/Sanitation/Waste Disposal/Property Rates rows carry their printed Sub Totals. Print A; kWh register plus a kVA register on some months; Property Rates and Waste Disposal sections. Checked on all 11 bills: 11/11 routed, identity gap R0.00 on 11/11, 0 checks, 0 steals; reading type is not printed on this municipality's bills; kVA only on 6 of 11 months.",
